        "original_id": "dca749c8-1835-5656-8e10-bbe79ee0ba04",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hudson Austin, Maurice Bishop, Bernard Coard, Eric Gairy\n- Organizations: New Jewel Movement\n- Places: Grenada\n- Roles: chairman, politician, leader, general\n- Events: 13 March 1979 revolution, coup, killing of Maurice Bishop\n\nFacts:\n- On 13 March 1979, the New Jewel Movement came to power in Grenada during a revolution that removed Eric Gairy from office.\n- Maurice Rupert Bishop was a Grenadian politician and the leader of the New Jewel Movement, which pursued socio-economic development, education, and Black liberation.\n- After Maurice Bishop was killed in 1983, Hudson Austin formed a military government in Grenada with himself as chairman.\n- Bernard Coard launched a coup within Grenada's revolutionary government and held power for three days until General Hudson Austin deposed him.",
